    "agent_last_message": "The tool is in `output/main.py`, run as `python main.py --input FILE --output FILE`. It uses only the standard library, and I tested it on Python 3.12.3. Python 3.11 isn't installed here, so I could only check that the code parses under the 3.11 grammar and uses no newer APIs.\n\nI also added `output/test_main.py`, a stdlib `unittest` suite, which you can run with `python -m unittest` from `output/`. All 75 tests pass in under a second. Each spec edge case is covered, along with every exit-code path. I also compared the tool against a separate whole-file implementation on 36,000 randomized inputs and read sizes, and it never differed.\n\nMeasured on 63\u2013105 MB files:\n\n| Input | Time | Peak memory |\n|---|---|---|\n| 105 MB natural-language text | 1.7 s | 28 MB |\n| 63 MB single line with no newlines | 0.9 s | 23 MB |\n| 63 MB with 5.8M distinct words (worst case) | 2.9 s | 751 MB |\n| One 84 MB word | 0.9 s | 252 MB |\n\nMemory grows with the number of distinct words, not with file size, so the all-distinct case is the expensive one.\n\nChoices the spec left open, which you may want to check:\n- **Invalid UTF-8 exits 1.** The spec counts bytes as characters, but `word` has to be a JSON string, so I treated non-UTF-8 input as \"malformed\". A Latin-1 file is rejected rather than approximated.\n- **Lowercasing is Unicode-aware**, so `\u00c9cole` and `\u00e9cole` count as one word. The spec only says \"lowercase\". If you want ASCII-only lowercasing, say so.\n- **Only the six ASCII whitespace characters split words**, as the spec lists them. A non-breaking space or an em space stays inside its word.\n- **Exit codes:**\n  - `argparse` normally exits 2 on bad usage, which your contract reserves for internal errors, so I changed it to 1. Abbreviated flags like `--inp` are rejected.\n  - An output path I can't open exits 1.\n  - A failure while writing the file, such as a full disk, exits 2.\n  - The output file is never created or touched when a run fails.\n- **Same-file guard (my addition):** the tool refus",
